{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/922446-dragon-blooded-investigation-ideas","id":922446,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Investigation Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T21:22:04-07:00","id":922446,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Investigation Ideas","content":"Just got done reading a scene in the <i>Sword Art Online: Progressive</i> manga (pretty much the only worthwhile branch of the franchise) where Asuna, Argo, and Kirito collectively work together to solve a mystery and convince a culprit to come clean about his crimes and his motivations.<br /> <br /> The trio work together naturally as a team. Whenever one of them strays off-course, another one senses that their conclusion rings false and yet finds within a spark of inspiration that leads them back to a correct conclusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elementary, My Dear Watson</b> -- whenever an ally fails an Investigation-based roll or a Read Intentions action, the Dragon-Blood adds the number of successes they managed to roll to his own Investigation or Awareness-based roll, or a Socialize-based Read Intentions, against the same target or scene.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <b>Good Catch!</b> -- as a special re-roll effect, if the Dragon-Blooded should fail to overcome the difficulty of an Investigation-based action or a Read Intentions action, one of his allies can add all of his successes to their own attempt; they also gain for free any Supplemental or Reflexive effects the Dragon-Blooded used to enhance the original action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar